you'd want to go into the source and find the definition for
dragonbane, then just change it there, then recompile:

This should work:

Get the source from nethack.org
Find the part of the source where it says the following:

A("Dragonbane",			BROADSWORD,
	(SPFX_RESTR|SPFX_DCLAS), 0, S_DRAGON,
	PHYS(5,0),	NO_DFNS,	NO_CARY,	0, A_NONE, NON_PM, NON_PM, 500L ),

change the word "BROADSWORD" to "LANCE", and that should work, so it'll
say:
A("Dragonbane",			LANCE,
	(SPFX_RESTR|SPFX_DCLAS), 0, S_DRAGON,
	PHYS(5,0),	NO_DFNS,	NO_CARY,	0, A_NONE, NON_PM, NON_PM, 500L ),

then compile it.

It's possible that it could still break, then you'd probably want to
find the part that describes lances breaking in general and remove it
